WEBVTT

00:03.910 --> 00:06.450
Ugh, I'm so tired.

00:06.450 --> 00:09.000
I only slept like, two hours yesterday.

00:09.000 --> 00:11.000
No way, what were you doing, you dirty girl?

00:11.000 --> 00:13.450
Ooh, who was a dirty girl?

00:13.450 --> 00:15.040
Seriously?

00:15.500 --> 00:16.910
Jeez, nothing like that!

00:16.910 --> 00:22.500
My boyfriend took me for a ride on the freeway,
and before we knew it, we were in Odaiba!

00:22.500 --> 00:23.580
Seriously?

00:23.580 --> 00:25.580
So you were up to something dirty, huh?

00:25.580 --> 00:28.250
You went to Tokyo?! Aw, man!

00:28.700 --> 00:31.540
When will I finally meet you?

00:31.750 --> 00:34.000
Ooh, Tomoya! He's so dreamy!

00:34.000 --> 00:35.080
Seriously.

00:35.080 --> 00:36.910
He's so cool...

00:36.910 --> 00:39.910
I heard Tomoya lived in Akeyuki
until like, middle school.

00:38.450 --> 00:41.700
Mommy
Tomorrow's your birthday, Nana-chan!
Dad got a reservation at a really nice place!
I hope you're looking forward to it!

00:39.910 --> 00:41.290
Really?

00:41.910 --> 00:44.660
I told her not to call him "Dad"...

00:44.660 --> 00:45.540
Huh?

00:45.540 --> 00:48.660
Oh, nothing! Tomoya's great, huh?

00:48.840 --> 00:55.840
Pushbard Matchmaking Service

00:49.200 --> 00:51.700
Let us go forth on a journey, together.

00:51.700 --> 00:53.620
The great journey of life.

00:53.620 --> 00:55.830
Pushbard Matchmaking Service.

02:29.830 --> 02:33.580
Hold on, did I hear that right?

02:33.750 --> 02:35.830
Because I feel like you just said,

02:35.830 --> 02:40.790
"The girl from yesterday was actually
me from a different world!"

02:41.540 --> 02:47.000
You know, I know that when you pretend to be
in some American TV show,

02:47.000 --> 02:49.080
you're just trying to make fun of me.

02:49.080 --> 02:51.410
I'm not trying to make fun of you!

02:51.410 --> 02:53.790
There's just no way I can agree with you on that!

02:53.790 --> 02:56.500
I'm having a hard time believing it, too...

02:56.500 --> 02:59.410
I mean, you did look pretty similar, but still...

02:59.410 --> 03:02.580
What about this, then? Isn't this proof?

03:03.330 --> 03:05.080
If she was just someone who looked like me,

03:05.080 --> 03:07.500
she wouldn't carry around
a picture of Kyo-chan, would she?!

03:07.500 --> 03:09.290
Umm, uh...

03:09.290 --> 03:11.370
Who's Kyo-chan?

03:11.370 --> 03:14.330
My little brother, Kyohei Tsuchimiya.

03:14.330 --> 03:16.040
Your little brother?

03:16.270 --> 03:17.950
That decides it.

03:17.950 --> 03:20.040
I support Asuka.

03:20.040 --> 03:22.040
What?! Chloe...

03:22.580 --> 03:25.790
We stumbled into a strange fantasy world yesterday,

03:26.410 --> 03:28.910
then met a girl who looked just like Asuka.

03:29.290 --> 03:31.200
Then there's this picture...

03:31.200 --> 03:33.620
It supports Asuka's theory.

03:33.750 --> 03:35.290
That's what I mean!

03:35.290 --> 03:36.250
So...

03:36.660 --> 03:40.580
We should do the 4:44 Ritual again!

03:40.790 --> 03:42.620
What?! Are you crazy?

03:42.620 --> 03:44.870
Do you remember the kind of danger
we were in yesterday?

03:44.870 --> 03:46.450
It'll be fine!

03:46.450 --> 03:47.540
Why?!

03:48.080 --> 03:51.200
Because Lord Chikuwa says it is!

03:52.660 --> 03:55.830
I'd feel a whole lot better if you just said
you had no idea why!

03:55.830 --> 03:58.450
We've got another mystery.

03:58.450 --> 04:00.910
Remember the noise I was hearing yesterday?

04:00.910 --> 04:02.370
It's gone.

04:02.370 --> 04:04.200
It's not on any frequency at all.

04:04.200 --> 04:09.580
The only reason the ritual worked was because
we used the frequency that we heard that noise on.

04:09.580 --> 04:13.000
I'll do something about that in ten minutes!

04:13.000 --> 04:13.950
Really?

04:14.040 --> 04:17.340
Asuka
We're gonna do the ritual again today!
Meet at the sacred tree!
I'm waiting for you!

04:19.040 --> 04:21.750
You there, miss.

04:19.370 --> 04:20.450
Fortunes

04:22.660 --> 04:25.200
You there, the very cute girl walking by!

04:25.200 --> 04:26.250
Wait, are you talking about me?

04:26.250 --> 04:28.450
I see something, yes...

04:28.450 --> 04:31.500
You are dissatisfied with your
current situation, yes?

04:31.500 --> 04:33.580
Especially when it comes to your family...

04:33.580 --> 04:35.000
W-wait, what?

04:35.000 --> 04:37.580
Look, tell me whatever you want,
I'm not gonna pay you.

04:37.870 --> 04:39.660
That is quite alright.

04:39.660 --> 04:44.120
I take pleasure in guiding those who are lost.

04:44.120 --> 04:47.450
I will now tell you a very special number.

04:48.500 --> 04:51.000
696.9.

04:51.000 --> 04:56.200
This number will lead you to
an undiscovered version of yourself...

04:58.120 --> 04:59.660
So...

05:00.040 --> 05:03.660
Maybe we should set the frequency to 696.9.

05:03.660 --> 05:05.870
Ooh, good idea, yeah!

05:05.870 --> 05:10.290
This is it! This is just what I needed,
this positive attitude!

05:10.290 --> 05:12.580
Well, sorry I was so negative, then.

05:12.580 --> 05:14.000
Are you sure about this, though?

05:14.000 --> 05:16.540
Should we use a frequency that we got
from some shady fortune teller?

05:16.540 --> 05:20.790
I mean, we've just been rolling some dice
for the ceremony this whole time...

05:21.450 --> 05:23.660
Frequency all set.

05:25.500 --> 05:28.830
Oh hey, the day after tomorrow's
your birthday, right, Nana?

05:28.830 --> 05:31.200
I'll let you do the important part of the spell!

05:31.200 --> 05:34.330
Wait, is that your idea of a birthday present?

05:34.500 --> 05:36.790
No, I'm gonna give you chikuwa, too.

05:36.870 --> 05:38.080
Yeah, I'll pass on that.

05:45.910 --> 05:50.620
Take us to the space that sleeps within the twilight.

06:01.040 --> 06:02.080
Huh?

06:02.330 --> 06:03.950
We're in the same place.

06:04.750 --> 06:06.750
It changed for a second, though...

06:07.040 --> 06:08.950
But it looks like we're back already.

06:09.750 --> 06:10.700
Um...

06:10.700 --> 06:12.700
Let's do it again, c'mon!

06:12.700 --> 06:14.700
It's 4:45 now.

06:14.700 --> 06:15.910
You're done.

06:16.270 --> 06:17.790
Why...?

06:17.790 --> 06:18.870
Hey, guys?

06:20.000 --> 06:22.120
Nana-senpai isn't here.

06:24.040 --> 06:25.120
Huh?

06:25.120 --> 06:26.160
Nana?

06:26.540 --> 06:28.120
Hey, Nana?

06:29.870 --> 06:32.330
What's wrong? You're staring off into space...

06:32.330 --> 06:36.580
Huh? Wait... Was that just a dream?

06:37.330 --> 06:40.250
And hold on, what are you wearing?
Is that some kind of cosplay?

06:40.250 --> 06:43.290
Huh? What are you talking about?

06:43.290 --> 06:44.950
Huh? Wait... What?!

06:46.250 --> 06:50.410
It looks like even Nana-senpai
gets nervous about it, too.

06:50.410 --> 06:52.410
I'm not surprised.

06:52.410 --> 06:55.410
She's going to experience the most important
part of a woman's life so very soon!

06:55.410 --> 06:57.410
What are they talking about...?

06:57.620 --> 07:01.120
Oh, hey, you're up after Nana, aren't you, Chloe?

07:01.120 --> 07:03.870
Huh? O-oh, well, I guess...

07:03.870 --> 07:07.120
Your birthday's in January, after all.

07:07.330 --> 07:10.290
Have you decided on the way
you're going to conduct your ceremony?

07:10.500 --> 07:13.450
Conduct? You mean, like, an orchestra, conduct?

07:13.620 --> 07:16.830
It's so hard to decide, huh. Go traditional,
or have a Western-style ceremony...

07:16.830 --> 07:19.660
A religious ceremony is best, hands down.

07:19.660 --> 07:22.950
Religious? Like, involving some kind of god?

07:23.160 --> 07:25.950
Your ceremony was so beautiful, Yu-senpai,

07:25.950 --> 07:28.750
dressed in all white and
performing those old traditions...

07:28.750 --> 07:30.160
Wait, what?

07:30.160 --> 07:32.540
Dressed in white doing a traditional performance?!

07:32.750 --> 07:34.910
I don't really care about that...

07:35.540 --> 07:40.540
I understand. It's the person you'll be standing
next to that's much more exciting, right?

07:40.540 --> 07:44.410
Oh, yeah! You've got your own fiancé,
now, don't you, Chloe-senpai?

07:44.410 --> 07:45.700
Well, yeah...

07:46.040 --> 07:47.540
Ii Naosuke?

07:47.540 --> 07:50.120
I think I heard about him in history class...

07:50.450 --> 07:52.790
Isn't he from like, the Edo Period?

07:53.200 --> 07:56.950
I've actually been thinking about
petitioning for exemption...

07:57.160 --> 08:01.950
Really? I hear it's super rare for those
to actually go through, though.

08:03.000 --> 08:07.450
Maybe, but... I don't think my heart is ready for it.

08:07.450 --> 08:12.660
I don't think mine was ready, either,
but honestly, my life isn't that bad.

08:12.660 --> 08:15.410
You seem really happy, Yu-senpai!

08:15.410 --> 08:18.950
It's almost like the two of you are doing
a giant puzzle together.

08:18.950 --> 08:21.000
It's so worth it.

08:21.000 --> 08:24.330
Though we might put pieces
in the wrong places sometimes.

08:24.500 --> 08:27.790
I'm busy enough with my own puzzle pieces...

08:28.120 --> 08:30.120
My, Nana-san, are you alright?

08:30.120 --> 08:34.450
Huh? Oh, no, I'm just thinking how sad it is,

08:34.450 --> 08:37.620
you know, how Ii Naosuke got assassinated
outside the Sakurada Gate.

08:40.120 --> 08:43.620
You're acting really strange, Nana-san.
Is everything alright?

08:43.620 --> 08:46.950
Huh? You guys are the ones who are acting weird!

08:46.950 --> 08:48.290
Especially you, Asuka.

08:48.290 --> 08:51.620
Why're you talking like that? It's super creepy.
Did you finally lose it?

08:51.620 --> 08:52.450
Oh, my...

08:52.450 --> 08:55.950
M-my goodness, Nana-senpai,
you shouldn't use such crude language...

08:55.950 --> 08:58.450
You're getting married in two days, you know!

08:58.450 --> 09:00.080
What does that have to do with anything?

09:02.120 --> 09:03.790
Wait, what did you just say?

09:04.160 --> 09:07.160
Nana... You know how it works, right?

09:07.700 --> 09:14.120
In two days, when you turn seventeen,
you have to get married...

09:14.620 --> 09:16.450
Married...?!

09:25.910 --> 09:31.580
Jeez, not only did Nana disappear,
but our bikes are gone, too! What the heck?!

09:31.580 --> 09:34.830
And my phone hasn't been able to get a signal...

09:32.370 --> 09:37.160
No Signal

09:34.830 --> 09:37.160
There's that, plus...

09:37.160 --> 09:38.870
Love
Charms

09:37.160 --> 09:40.120
Does the town feel weird to anyone else?

09:38.870 --> 09:42.610
Honeymoon Trips

09:40.120 --> 09:42.620
Yeah, there's something off...

09:46.200 --> 09:47.580
Look over here!

09:47.580 --> 09:49.290
Those are our bikes!

09:49.540 --> 09:54.200
So you bike-stealing bastards
were having a cup of tea at Octave, huh?!

09:55.450 --> 09:57.040
What are you talking about?!

09:57.040 --> 09:58.830
What do you mean, married?

09:58.830 --> 10:01.330
Why do I have to get married?!

10:01.540 --> 10:04.950
There's Nana! Thank god!

10:05.120 --> 10:08.000
There's no point in asking why... Right?

10:08.330 --> 10:13.580
The law says that all women have to be
married on their seventeenth birthday.

10:13.580 --> 10:16.790
Whyever are you so upset?
Especially now, of all times...

10:16.790 --> 10:21.120
Perhaps she's experiencing an unstable mental state
that accompanies premarital depression?

10:21.120 --> 10:23.830
W-w-w-wait, is that...

10:23.830 --> 10:26.290
Us... Right?

10:26.290 --> 10:28.120
What in the world?! Why?!

10:28.330 --> 10:32.040
I can only think of one reason
why there are two of us...

10:32.410 --> 10:35.410
You're in a different world.

10:35.410 --> 10:37.330
Hey! It's me!

10:38.410 --> 10:41.790
Why are you here? How did you follow me?

10:41.790 --> 10:44.830
Well, we did the 4:44 Ritual...

10:44.830 --> 10:47.040
How did you know the right frequency?!

10:47.040 --> 10:51.040
Nana-senpai got it from some weird fortune-teller lady...

10:51.040 --> 10:52.330
A fortune-teller...?

10:54.620 --> 10:57.080
You should go home and rest.

10:57.080 --> 10:59.080
You'll feel right as rain, Nana-san.

10:59.790 --> 11:02.910
Nooo, I'm taking Nana somewhere...

11:02.910 --> 11:04.040
Stay hidden for now.

11:04.450 --> 11:08.330
It will cause all sorts of problems
if you're seen by yourselves.

11:08.330 --> 11:09.750
You're right.

11:09.750 --> 11:13.000
For now, we have some things we'd like to ask you.

11:19.870 --> 11:22.870
I suppose I can't keep it from you any longer...

11:23.750 --> 11:26.200
My name is Asuka Tsuchimiya.

11:26.200 --> 11:30.370
I'm the same Asuka, but from a parallel world.

11:38.810 --> 11:42.790
Parallel Worlds
Possibilities

11:39.290 --> 11:42.790
I'm sure you've heard of divergent timelines before.

11:43.500 --> 11:44.500
Nope.

11:45.700 --> 11:47.580
What about parallel worlds?

11:47.580 --> 11:49.950
Ooh, yes! I think so!

11:49.950 --> 11:52.200
Forget her, just keep going.

11:52.200 --> 11:54.410
Right. Think of it like this:

11:54.510 --> 12:01.270
Possibility

11:55.040 --> 12:00.700
Every possibility creates numerous
parallel timelines, or worlds.

12:01.580 --> 12:07.000
The possibilities in each of those worlds create
branches, and those create branches themselves...

12:07.330 --> 12:11.580
As such, there are more parallel worlds
than there are stars in the sky.

12:12.080 --> 12:15.540
The world you live in is one of those worlds.

12:15.910 --> 12:18.790
So right now, we're in a different world.

12:18.790 --> 12:22.450
Right. We call them "fragments".

12:22.790 --> 12:27.200
This world split off from your world
about ten years ago.

12:27.200 --> 12:29.500
It's a relatively close fragment.

12:29.700 --> 12:34.000
Umm, why did Nana-senpai get separated from us?

12:34.290 --> 12:39.370
That's probably because she was the first person
to move in this world. Am I right?

12:39.370 --> 12:41.200
You know, now that you mention it...

12:44.870 --> 12:52.450
As such, she was assimilated into her parallel self,
becoming a link between your group and this world.

12:52.450 --> 12:53.910
A link?

12:53.910 --> 13:01.160
This link allows you to exist within this world,
as well as return to your world.

13:01.450 --> 13:08.200
So that means that every time we go to a parallel world,
one of us will have to be the link.

13:08.200 --> 13:11.330
This time, it was Nana... Am I right?

13:11.330 --> 13:14.000
Yes, that's a good way to put it.

13:14.000 --> 13:20.000
So the people of this world will think
that Nana-senpai is a fake...

13:20.000 --> 13:21.830
I hope she'll be okay...

13:22.080 --> 13:25.870
Luckily, people are strongly affected
by their normalcy bias.

13:27.540 --> 13:32.330
They tend to ignore deviations from the norm
if doing so would be in their favor.

13:33.540 --> 13:38.160
Thanks to that bias, nobody should come to
believe that she is not the real Nana.

13:40.080 --> 13:41.500
I'm home.

13:41.500 --> 13:43.080
Welcome home, honey.

13:45.620 --> 13:48.950
Thank god, Mom hasn't changed at all...

13:48.950 --> 13:51.410
Are you alright, Nana-chan?

13:51.410 --> 13:54.870
I just received a startling phone call
from one of your friends.

13:54.870 --> 13:58.330
Ugh, no. Everyone's being like, so frickin' weird.

13:58.330 --> 14:01.080
Like, they kept saying I was gonna
get married tomorrow, or something.

14:01.080 --> 14:02.080
Oh, my gosh...

14:02.080 --> 14:05.450
Come on, who gets married at seventeen?

14:05.450 --> 14:07.290
This isn't some period drama.

14:08.040 --> 14:09.450
Nana-chan...

14:09.910 --> 14:12.080
Why are you speaking like that?

14:12.080 --> 14:14.410
Did you watch a movie about
delinquent girls or some nonsense?

14:15.290 --> 14:17.580
You're soon to be married! Now is not the time!

14:17.580 --> 14:18.410
What?

14:18.410 --> 14:20.370
Well, it's alright. Come hither, now.

14:20.370 --> 14:23.040
Dad came home early today!

14:23.370 --> 14:26.660
So I really am gonna get married...?

14:27.870 --> 14:30.160
Welcome home, Nana-chan!

14:30.160 --> 14:32.160
Look, I got you a present!

14:32.500 --> 14:34.790
Huh? Why are you giving this to me today?

14:34.790 --> 14:40.750
Well, I'll be home late from work tomorrow, and you
won't have time for this the day after, now will you?

14:40.750 --> 14:42.040
I wonder what it could be!

14:44.330 --> 14:46.910
Oh, my, look, they match!

14:46.910 --> 14:49.120
Great, isn't it? I had it made special for you.

14:49.120 --> 14:51.370
See? It's got your name,
and your husband's name, too...

14:51.370 --> 14:52.700
This is creepy.

14:53.040 --> 14:53.950
Huh?

14:54.620 --> 14:56.540
This is all so creepy!

14:56.540 --> 15:00.500
These matching clothes, calling me "Nana-chan",

15:01.040 --> 15:03.950
marrying off your underage daughter!

15:04.160 --> 15:05.910
It's really frickin' creepy!

15:07.540 --> 15:11.540
Come on, admit it, you've been super annoyed
by me these last three years, right?

15:11.540 --> 15:16.450
I mean, you can't help but remember
my real dad when I'm around, huh?!

15:17.160 --> 15:18.160
Nana!

15:18.160 --> 15:22.370
That's why you want to marry me off quick
and get me out of the house, huh?

15:22.370 --> 15:26.250
Else, you wouldn't be marrying off
your seventeen-year-old daughter!

15:26.250 --> 15:27.250
But the law says-

15:27.250 --> 15:28.500
Whatever!

15:28.500 --> 15:31.080
He wouldn't try to make me happy
with some matching shirts!

15:31.080 --> 15:33.950
He wouldn't let me get away with my crappy grades!

15:33.950 --> 15:37.040
He wouldn't just let me dye my hair
whatever color I wanted!

15:37.620 --> 15:40.750
If my real dad was here...

15:41.540 --> 15:44.370
he'd care a whole lot more about me!

15:53.950 --> 15:55.950
Yeah, who is it?

15:59.250 --> 16:01.660
Sorry I'm five minutes late.

16:01.660 --> 16:04.660
Sometimes, I just want to see what you
look like when you're angry.

16:04.950 --> 16:07.450
What? Tomoya Chiba...?

16:07.450 --> 16:09.500
Come in, Tomoya-san!

16:09.500 --> 16:12.330
Hello, Mom. I'm sorry to bother you
right before the ceremony,

16:12.330 --> 16:14.580
but I'm going to borrow Nana-san for a bit.

16:14.580 --> 16:16.160
Huh? Wait, so you mean...

16:16.160 --> 16:20.330
What? Did you forget what your
future husband looked like?

16:22.910 --> 16:24.700
Yu-senpai, come eat!

16:26.450 --> 16:29.410
What's this all about?
I mean, I know why we've got chikuwa...

16:29.700 --> 16:31.950
I found them in the break room kitchen.

16:31.950 --> 16:35.040
The manju were on the vice principal's desk.

16:35.040 --> 16:39.080
I was so scared the security guard would see us!

16:39.410 --> 16:42.450
You guys are adapting really well to this.

16:42.450 --> 16:43.950
The logic behind it doesn't matter.

16:43.950 --> 16:48.620
We've still got to accept the fact
that we're in a different world.

16:48.620 --> 16:52.250
I mean, I get why we're here, but...

16:52.370 --> 16:55.450
To be honest, I don't really understand it well...

16:55.450 --> 16:59.830
But you heard what that Asuka-senpai girl said, right?

17:00.370 --> 17:07.120
Don't worry. If you do the Ritual of 4:44 again,
you can return to your world.

17:07.540 --> 17:12.080
No time will have passed, so nobody
will think you were missing at all.

17:12.450 --> 17:16.620
We can go back to our world,
without having anyone worrying about us.

17:16.620 --> 17:19.620
So maybe it's alright to just go with the flow here.

17:19.830 --> 17:23.000
I wish I could be as optimistic as you are, Mia.

17:23.000 --> 17:24.040
Same.

17:24.410 --> 17:26.540
There's one thing that still doesn't
make sense, though.

17:26.540 --> 17:27.410
What?

17:27.410 --> 17:32.000
She told us all that stuff about parallel worlds,

17:32.000 --> 17:34.080
but she left out one thing.

17:35.250 --> 17:38.160
She didn't tell us what she's doing here.

17:39.540 --> 17:40.790
Here.

17:41.000 --> 17:42.870
I can't believe you forgot it.

17:42.870 --> 17:44.700
It's really important to you, isn't it?

17:45.000 --> 17:46.200
Yeah.

17:46.910 --> 17:49.580
Is his name Kyo-chan on your side, too?

17:49.580 --> 17:51.870
Yeah. Kyohei.

17:54.830 --> 18:00.080
In my world, when Kyo-chan was six,
he suddenly disappeared.

18:00.370 --> 18:04.700
The police and all the neighbors
looked for him, but we couldn't find him.

18:05.080 --> 18:06.750
We never did.

18:06.750 --> 18:08.370
What happened in your world?

18:09.120 --> 18:12.250
It happened in my world when he was six, too.

18:15.250 --> 18:16.410
Okay.

18:18.250 --> 18:19.750
Oh, hey!

18:19.750 --> 18:23.580
It's super confusing with us both being called Asuka,
so why don't we change things up?

18:23.580 --> 18:26.080
I really don't care... What's your idea?

18:26.080 --> 18:30.700
Let's see. You're like, way more
serious than I am, right?

18:30.700 --> 18:32.290
So how about...

18:32.290 --> 18:33.410
Seriousuka!

18:33.410 --> 18:34.250
No.

18:34.250 --> 18:35.950
Aww, come on!

18:35.950 --> 18:37.290
I said, no.

18:37.870 --> 18:39.540
Hey, who's there?!

18:50.250 --> 18:53.660
This is truly a miracle. No, fate, even.

18:53.660 --> 18:54.540
Huh?

18:54.750 --> 18:59.500
I only signed up on that matchmaking site
because it was in my commercial contract.

18:59.830 --> 19:04.000
I never thought that it would lead me
to an amazing girl like you.

19:04.500 --> 19:05.950
Tomoya-san...?

19:06.660 --> 19:07.620
Nana...

19:10.790 --> 19:12.000
N-no!

19:13.290 --> 19:16.290
Sorry, I'll hold back for today.

19:16.290 --> 19:21.330
I'd rather kiss you two days from now,
when the whole world will bless our union.

19:21.330 --> 19:23.080
The whole world?

19:23.080 --> 19:24.450
That's an exaggeration, right?

19:24.450 --> 19:25.870
Of course not!

19:25.870 --> 19:29.870
Our wedding will be broadcast live
on television and streamed online.

19:30.120 --> 19:34.700
Everyone around the world will see us
and experience our love...

19:36.000 --> 19:38.000
And the happiness we will share.

19:40.080 --> 19:41.080
Nana...

19:43.580 --> 19:47.000
Let us go forth on a journey, together.

19:47.330 --> 19:49.370
The great journey of life...

19:50.410 --> 19:51.830
Tomoya-san...

19:56.540 --> 19:58.870
Ohmigosh, is that Tomoya Chiba?!

19:59.750 --> 20:02.040
No way, for real?! Where?!

20:02.040 --> 20:04.000
Uh-oh, looks like I've been spotted.

20:04.000 --> 20:06.080
Tomoya! Can I get your autograph?!

20:06.080 --> 20:07.830
Can I get a selfie with you?!

20:07.830 --> 20:10.750
Sorry, girls, I'm in the middle of something right now!

20:10.750 --> 20:11.910
C'mon, let's go!

20:12.620 --> 20:14.370
Aww, there he goes!

20:20.080 --> 20:23.830
Are you sure it's okay to show up
this late at night, asking to stay over?

20:23.830 --> 20:27.080
We don't want to surprise Nana-senpai's parents...

20:27.080 --> 20:31.540
Nana will know who we are! It'll be fine.

20:32.790 --> 20:34.410
Can I ask you something?

20:34.580 --> 20:35.870
Depends on the question.

20:36.080 --> 20:40.620
Why are you traveling to parallel worlds
outside of your own?

20:41.660 --> 20:44.000
I'm looking for something.

20:44.750 --> 20:45.580
And what-

20:45.580 --> 20:48.000
That what is none of your business.

20:52.620 --> 20:54.500
Hey, guys, stop!

20:56.830 --> 20:59.580
It's Nana! And a real fancy car...

20:59.580 --> 21:02.080
Is that her boyfriend? Nana has a boyfriend?!

21:02.950 --> 21:06.000
I'll see you at the chapel in two days, Nana-chan.

21:06.000 --> 21:08.080
Yeah... See you there.

21:16.250 --> 21:17.830
Nana! Nana!

21:18.160 --> 21:20.290
Oh, hey, guys...

21:20.450 --> 21:22.620
I'm so glad you're okay!

21:22.910 --> 21:25.910
I'm sorry about all the weird things I said before.

21:25.910 --> 21:28.410
Huh? What'd you say again?

21:28.410 --> 21:32.870
Remember? I asked if you were crazy, and talked about
the Sakurada assassination, all that weird stuff.

21:32.870 --> 21:34.370
Huh? What?

21:34.660 --> 21:37.700
I think she thinks we're the other us.

21:37.700 --> 21:39.290
I think you're right...

21:39.660 --> 21:42.950
I was kind of spaced out this whole afternoon...

21:42.950 --> 21:45.290
But I've gotten my bearings,
and I feel much better now.

21:45.700 --> 21:48.200
I think my heart is ready.

21:49.540 --> 21:55.660
In two days, on the day of my seventeenth birthday,

21:55.660 --> 21:58.330
I, Nana Nanase, will marry Tomoya Chiba!
